> To be honest, I find Valks to be kinda boring overall. My favorite
> classes to play are Samurai, Wizard, Knight, and Monk. Which of
> those do you think would fare best in a quick ascension?

Wizards. But wizards should probably be played a bit different from
the others. I suggest Samurais as well. But if you are bored of
valkyries then you will find samurais boring as well, especially if
you get past the early game and discover the samurai's two-weaponing
power. Monks are again quite a bit different from the others; so I
wouldn't play them if you want to learn some wider applicable tactics.

> 
>> I'd suggest to watch also non-ascension games. You'll probably learn
>> from (observed and own) mistakes more than from pure ascension games.
> 
> Are there any specific ones you can recommend? I wouldn't even know
> where to begin looking in the NAO archive.

No, I cannot, or rather don't want to recommend anyone specific.[*]
You don't need to browse the archives, rather look at the actually
played games. Observe the player's tactics and their mistakes. If
you have doubts why a player has done some specific action, just
send him a mail message in-game; many players will certainly answer
your questions kindly.

If you're focussed on specific classes, as it seems, I'd have a look
at NAO's ascension list (http://alt.org/nethack/mostascensions.html)
and pick those players that are also focussed on a specific class.
You'll find a lot who play (and ascend) wizards (stth, cstaub67, eg.),
for monks you may refer to the archive records of Erokh (he's inactive
at the moment), the tourist expert is PaRaD0xx (still active)[**].

